{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1459105-playing-ctd-purely-as-a-fae","id":1459105,"title":"Playing CTD purely as a Fae?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-07T01:21:58-07:00","id":1459105,"title":"Playing CTD purely as a Fae?","content":"Is it possible to play CTD purely as a Fae, instead of having any association with being a Human/Changeling? I just don't like being so heavily tied down to the human aspect of things and what makes me love the WoD franchise in general, is the part where you character is a supernatural being. CTD I feel, has a too much of a weird mix where your human side is so overemphasized in some areas over your Fae aspect; where to a part I just want to be all Fae.<br /> <br /> How would being only a Fae and not a Changeling work for the game?<br /> <br /> How would CTD function if you change up its story, where there was no Changing Way at all and instead all the Fae went back to the Dreaming, but came back with the Rocket Launch and begin re-exploring the Autumn World? Or where the Changing Way was never developed, but some Fae still remained on Earth?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T04:49:02-07:00","id":1459118,"title":"","content":"Look into the Dark Kin. They didn't come back after the moon landing, but rather after the Reckoning (circa 1999); but they're representative of what a pure fae in the modern world would be like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T05:09:18-07:00","id":1459123,"title":"","content":"The obvious option for baseline CTD is the Inanimae - while they're very much _affected_ by humanity, they're not, and never have been, human. They get by in the human world by having their material bodies pass for human as best they can.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, just give Dark Ages: Fae a setting update (although that one requires the Dark Ages: Vampire book for rules). The splats there are Firstborn (fully fae), Inanimae (elemental fae), and Changeling (human-touched fae/fae-touched human - not fae in human body, as with CTD).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T05:12:18-07:00","id":1459124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1459105-playing-ctd-purely-as-a-fae?p=1459118#post1459118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look into the Dark Kin. They didn't come back after the moon landing, but rather after the Reckoning (circa 1999); but they're representative of what a pure fae in the modern world would be like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing there is that they still require human bodies to properly interact with the Autumn World - most handle this by possessing humans, but some have access to a human body that's entirely theirs.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ah, hadn't refreshed my memory on the C20 writeup, where they can manifest in physical form by spending Glamour, but are left vulnerable to Banality, which manifests as them taking physical damage from it until they return to the Dreaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":51,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","user":"marin","date":". 09-07-2021, 08:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T05:32:10-07:00","id":1459126,"title":"","content":"Well, yes; given how hostile the Autumn World is to pure fae, you need <i>some</i> sort of \u201cenvironmental suit\u201d in order to enter such a toxic environment and survive. But for the Dark Kin, those \u201csuits\u201c are a temporary measure: they only need to use them when they want to physically interact with the Autumn World. When they're restricting their activities to dealing with chimerical reality, they need not bother with them at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T14:38:05-07:00","id":1459192,"title":"","content":"Besides, it is up to each individual ST to decide how much emphasis they put on your human side. For example the Sidhe, who tend to live in Freeholds to avoid aging and Banality, sometimes only barely care for their human sides as is and focus more on Fae matters. Chronicles that are either set in the Dreaming, or that lean heavily towards Dreaming and Chimerical side of things, can ignore the human side almost entirely. It all depends on the mood you want. CtD can be played with heavy leaning to the human side which brings it\u2019s own kinds of stories, about Banality versus Glamour and people seeing you as unhinged or completely insane. But it does not have to be.<br /> <br /> This is part of the reason I love CtD so much it gives me the tools and the reason to play so totally different games within the same game. Even with the same characters and the same story if one wishes. Your tale might begin from you struggling within human society, trying to avoid Banality and desperately trying to appear sane to your friends and family even though you can see the other reality all around you to which they are completely blind. And then the story might take a turn and you have to leave them behind for a quest within the Dreaming where your humanity is but a fleeting dream as your Fae side gets stronger and stronger and the game becomes more and more wildly fantastic. And after finishing your quest and returning to the cold reality and the harshness of a banal human existence in a world where you have been missing for hours/days/years/decades no matter how long or short your foray to the Dreaming was. No other game can give you all this in one gorgeous package.<br /> <br /> Talk to your ST and make the game and the story you and your group want. All the tools are already there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T21:55:03-07:00","id":1459253,"title":"","content":"Going only C20:<br /> <br /> - Ignoring your human side is completely feasible, plenty of Changelings do that. Ignoring the Autumn World completely is what is really problematic, but doesn't seem to be your point;<br /> <br /> - As said before, Inanimae and Dark Kin are pure fae and the rules for them are in the core book;<br /> <br /> - Finally, it is really easy to apply a Kith to the rules of Dark Kin and get yourself what is mechanically a Kithain without a human soul. In thesis a good chunk of House Danaan are like that anyway.<br /> <br /> Although it was never stated to exist, a non-Changeling Kithain isn't strictly impossible by the lore. They could have existed in some form of suspension in the Dreaming, or they may have come from Arcadia recently for whatever reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T07:30:05-07:00","id":1459553,"title":"","content":"<br /> Dark Kin versions of the Kithain would be neat. There was one for Dark Kin Redcaps floating around awhile ago. Having this as an option for Arcadian fae that returned with the Sidhe would fit well.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T20:20:16-07:00","id":1459617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1459105-playing-ctd-purely-as-a-fae?p=1459553#post1459553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dark Kin versions of the Kithain would be neat. There was one for Dark Kin Redcaps floating around awhile ago. Having this as an option for Arcadian fae that returned with the Sidhe would fit well.</div> </div> </div> </div>On all seriousness, it is just a matter of applying the section &quot;Denizens and the Autumn World&quot;, C20 pp 385, to a Kith. All their other particular rules aren't tied to them being in the dreaming but to them not being a Kithain to begin with. Reading the Ari\u00e1 can give you a sense of how to turn up the interpretation of your Court, but since the Court system is actually pre-Sundering, there is no need for further tinkering beyond that.<br /> <br /> For rules, use the Possession Rede, pp 322, and you're good to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T02:32:02-07:00","id":1459636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1459105-playing-ctd-purely-as-a-fae?p=1459192#post1459192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example the Sidhe, who tend to live in Freeholds to avoid aging and Banality, sometimes only barely care for their human sides as is and focus more on Fae matters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't the Bedlam mechanism prevent this? From C20, p294: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Changelings dread Banality, but they fear Bedlam. Conven-<br /> tional wisdom among the Kithain describes Bedlam as madness<br /> caused by overexposure to the Dreaming. An abundance of time<br /> spent in particularly Banal places or without reminders of the<br /> character\u2019s fae nature leads to becoming Undone, but saturation<br /> in Glamour beyond what the changeling\u2019s mortal seeming can<br /> withstand propels the changeling into Bedlam. The road to<br /> Bedlam is marked with many signs and warnings, called Bedlam<br /> Thresholds, as the chimerical world intrudes on the changeling\u2019s<br /> senses and obstructs her interactions with the Autumn realm. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T09:41:48-07:00","id":1459665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1459105-playing-ctd-purely-as-a-fae?p=1459636#post1459636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't the Bedlam mechanism prevent this? From C20, p294:</div> </div> </div> </div>By RAW, not really. When it comes to the rule on this, it is just a Nightmare Die every week spent entirely in the Freehold.<br /> <br /> So the Changeling doesn't really have to care about human-side things, just walk down the street once in a while, maybe sleep over at a hotel once or twice a week.<br /> <br /> Even a house that isn't a Freehold <i>per se</i> is enough without any need to have humans or human-related things on them.<br /> <br /> The noble may evade Bedlam by jogging at a park everyday and keeping a mansion retreat outside the Freehold for the weekends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T12:44:44-07:00","id":1459679,"title":"","content":"monteparnas beat me to it, but yeah by RAW Bedlam is tied to your Nightmare Dice and you get those from a straight week spend in a Freehold/Dreaming, by botching a Cantrip and through Unleashing.<br /> <br /> My last C20 game was almost entirely in the Dreaming, though it did begin in the Autumn world but even there it was mostly Fae business, and Bedlam was only issue/danger for one player but he was a bit more liberal with the Unleashings than the rest of the group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-15T01:48:51-07:00","id":1460008,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, it seems to me that spending a few hours out of the dreaming every week in order to get around the rules is a bit meta-gaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-15T07:06:14-07:00","id":1460028,"title":"","content":"Not quite, either, because this is more or less common in-game knowledge. They wouldn't reason it out that specifically, but Changeling society knows that spending too much time at once without getting a little fresh air in the Autumn World ain't good for you. Once every 3 or 4 days wouldn't be an unreasonable rule of thumb.<br /> <br /> Of course, you can and should make it harder if you feel the need, IIRC the rules don't restrict Nightmare Dice only to those situations, they just don't require more than that, is a big difference. Starting in the easy mode and letting the ST crank up from there helps making the game more versatile, precisely because it gives space to the many chronicles where too much mundanity just gets in the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T18:11:42-07:00","id":1462370,"title":"","content":"I like this question because as an ST I want to have NPCs like this - actual fae who are not Changelings - in the setting. I think this is what most people expected the game to be about back when White Wolf said they were planning for &quot;Faerie&quot; instead of &quot;Changeling&quot;. After giving this some thought, below are the salient points I can think of. I welcome anyone giving corrections or comments because CTD is the main WoD game I am least familiar with.<br /> <br /> Such fae should be considered to be Sentient Animate Chimera. That's what Sprites are, and I feel they would be examples of real fae that have not undergone the Changeling way. And that is what the other creatures of the Dreaming are considered to be. Likely we would need to adopt a new classification for these natural born chimera if there isn't a term already available. Fairies traditionally don't have children of their own. It happens, but is rare. That is why they need to steal human children or have human lovers. So the setting would need to address that. Perhaps a fairy parent can only ever have one fae child, meaning 2 parents can only produce 1 child which is way under the replacement rate. Or there's some other reason why such children are very rare. On the plus side, these fae are naturally immortal like the siochain. Still they can be killed. So over time, such fae population would go into decline. This is why kinain and changelings need to be produced for the fae race to not go extinct.<br /> <br /> In lieu of rules for creating Chimera PCs, likely just use the normal Chimera creation rules and use 35 points for a new character. However, since Chimera normally don't have Arts &amp; Realms just Redes, we'd need to figure something out. Or determine whether such Fae have access to both Redes and Arts/Realms. And how XP translate into &quot;chimera points.&quot; But I think if an ST really wanted this as an option she can crunch the rules enough to figure out how to do it properly for PCs. Wanting to have splats for Chimera PCs would probably just be an exercise in grouping together various tropes together and assigning Birthrights and Frailities together.<br /> <br /> Such Chimerical Fae would spend most of their time in the Dreaming, not the Autumn Realm. The few times they interact with mortals would probably be when a mortal enters one of the transitional zones like a Freehold. However, they still need a power that enables them to go out when they want. Redes like Wyrd and Enchantment can do that. ST would need to decide whether these are innate powers all Chimerical Fae would have, or whether they would need to be bought first. Issues with Banality do exist, but are already covered in the Chimera section.<br /> <br /> Such a game would probably have most of the PCs spending their time in the Near Dreaming or another part of the Dreaming. Issues like Bedlam wouldn't exist. You can a fun game just playing there, but I think it loses that World of Darkness feel if they don't have a reason to interact with the mortals and beings of the Autumn World. There probably still needs to be some kind of need to deal with the Autumn World because Banality needs to somehow intrude and harm the fae world. Maybe the Near Dreaming is somehow being eroded which would only leave the Far Dreaming left and eventually that would be threatened. And the only way to fight it would be somehow to go out and quest in the Autumn World. Perhaps not so much to defeat Banality, but defend those few Freeholds left from being destroyed by it.<br /> <br /> Changelings as a character type still have an important role. First, they understand the Autumn World better and can better do those quests than the Chimerical Fae can. They have to work together. In contrast, Chimera PCs can better participate in the Dreaming and can help the Changelings with that. But I think a major part of the setting would be in describing how bits of the Near Dreaming are falling to the black, or whatever euphemism/trademark/term that would be used to describe it. Maybe rules for how freeholds decline in rank. Something an ST can do to make the loss apparent to the PCs. The rise of Banality might manifest in the Dreaming as something similar to the Nothing in Fantastica in the Neverending Story. I think it'd be important for Banality to be a force you can't hide from, but which will intrude into the Dreaming to devastating effect. and that the connection between the Autumn World and the Dreaming still has to be maintained. It's just brainstorming ideas that can translate that into events and actions for the PCs.<br /> <br /> Lastly, there would need to be some kind of actual ritual that explains how one of these chimerical fae can become a Changeling. It's all good and fine to say &quot;the Changing way&quot; exists to explain how the transition initially occurred. But once chimerical Fae come into play, there needs to be an actual ritual or mechanic that explains the transfer for flavor text purposes if nothing else. The benefit would be greater protection from Banality. They price would be Bedlam and the loss of natural immortality for perpetual reincarnation (unless siochain status is achieved).<br /> <br /> I think having chimerical Fae and Changelings side by side would change a lot of the game. Most of the nobility would probably be on the Dreaming side of things. There can still be Sidhe nobles as Changelings, but they'd be more like the black sheep of the family than kings and queens. But being a knight errant would still be cool. Maybe a limit to the noble title a changeling could hold - like count. Everything else would belong to the chimerical fae. Instead of having there be a commoner - noble conflict, it'd be more a changeling vs chimerical fae conflict in society.<br /> <br /> Does that make sense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T18:31:13-07:00","id":1462371,"title":"","content":"In light of this, consider the Lyceans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T19:56:33-07:00","id":1462383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1459105-playing-ctd-purely-as-a-fae?p=1462370#post1462370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does that make sense?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sense it makes, but most of those questions were already addressed by the setting and contradict your proposal. Since you said you're not very familiar with it, I'll shortly explain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1459105-playing-ctd-purely-as-a-fae?p=1462370#post1462370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Such fae should be considered to be Sentient Animate Chimera</div> </div> </div> </div>The setting already have well defined that fae and chimera aren't exactly the same thing, although chimera can evolve into actual fairies, one example being the Wolpertinger Kith, a former type of chimera that recently started to become Kithain.<br /> <br /> But it is also well established that the Kithain already followed most of the same rules and had the same Arts and Realms before the Changeling Way. And also, there are already other types of fairies that aren't changelings, but completely fae, the Inanimae and Dark Kin, with proper, well defined rules. In lore there is also at least one group of Sidhe that didn't underwent the Changeling Way yet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1459105-playing-ctd-purely-as-a-fae?p=1462370#post1462370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Likely we would need to adopt a new classification for these natural born chimera if there isn't a term already available. Fairies traditionally don't have children of their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chimera form naturally all the time and fairies can reproduce just fine. Although it doesn't seems to be frequent, it was never stated as a problem and the greater challenge now is that the child of two Changelings may be just Kinain, but it can also be an entirely new Kithain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1459105-playing-ctd-purely-as-a-fae?p=1462370#post1462370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, they still need a power that enables them to go out when they want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chimera can walk into the Autumn World and actually many live exclusively there. Being invisible and intangible for humans don't affect them that much. What's more, as long as no human is watching they can interact with the world to some extent, the book isn't clear on how much, but to me it seemed that they just can interact as normal with unseen physical objects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1459105-playing-ctd-purely-as-a-fae?p=1462370#post1462370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But once chimerical Fae come into play, there needs to be an actual ritual or mechanic that explains the transfer for flavor text purposes if nothing else.</div> </div> </div> </div>That kind of already exists. Although the Changeling Way <i>per se</i> isn't explained, most of the stuff happening is well defined:<br /> <br /> Kithain can hollow out a human body and take it. The human soul is sent to Arcadia, something most Sidhe consider a high prize to give them. Not everyone is so optimistic, but no one can really do something about it. It isn't complex and no rolls are given, the Changeling-to-be just chose the mortal and do it.<br /> <br /> Changeling Way is a secondary step. Once you have a human body you can make the ritual to become half-human in a next reincarnation. If you don't, no one knows what happens to your soul. The ritual lacks details, but is hinted to be simple, the biggest challenge being the decision to do it itself.<br /> <br /> Dark Kin can possess mortals, but their possession is temporary and does nothing to the human soul. Except, well, traumatic experiences. There is also no roll, which I think was probably an oversight as they are playable and all their rules are given. They can also simply Materialize for a shorter stay in the Autumn World.<br /> <br /> Inanimae can form physical forms out of their own element, similar to how Dark Kin Materialize but far sturdier. They do have enough rules for everything they do and they don't do things like the Changeling Way or possessing humans.<br /> <br /> Nunnehi and Menehune have their own variation on the Changeling Way that responds for some of their distinct rules, but it is essentially the same thing and compatible, the Menehune even learned it from the Kithain directly. Hsien were cursed with the Changeling Way instead, so to speak, although they seem to actually be something else and not fae at all. They really strike me as Angels that got partially screwed some time after the Fallen being imprisoned in Hell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1459105-playing-ctd-purely-as-a-fae?p=1462370#post1462370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There can still be Sidhe nobles as Changelings, but they'd be more like the black sheep of the family than kings and queens. But being a knight errant would still be cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Curiously in lore most of House Danaan still live in the Dreaming and are completely fae, but they are the ones acting more as knight errant there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T17:18:28-07:00","id":1462944,"title":"","content":"As has been said, what the OP is describing is just the Denizens. Or at least that's the situation now, they're pure non-human fae spirits who are offended by the idea of pretending to be pitiful ape meatsacks to fit in. The old Denizen book even went into the conflict over whether the Fae should hide themselves from humans, or cow humans back into awed submission.<br /> The other part is, as with all WW writing, taking the mythology presented as objective truth is perhaps not the best idea, even within the splat. Accepting DA Fae, the current Changeling Commoners at least, were all just Sprites/Spirits/Chimera before the Shattering broke the Umbra into myth/culture specific versions of everything. It's likely the modern Sidhe were nothing more than Chimera the Summer Court took with them when they got booted off Earth along with the other three &quot;Fomorian&quot; courts.<br /> If you tinker with the cookie cutter version of Kiths the books present, you just have to keep in mind that the rest of the setting is just the current beliefs and theories of the splat in question, and adjust accordingly. Did the Umbra break apart into everyone's personal Otherworld, did the conflict with the &quot;Fomorians&quot; about hiding/cowing simply go the other way, and if so, is it the current &quot;Tuatha/Arcadian&quot; proponents of hiding who got labeled Fomorian and are currently holding the Evil ball?<br /> Also, DA Fae did in fact explain the original means by which Sprites/Chimera became true Fae, complete with dice rolls, and gave a real purpose to Saining.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25819-wrxsv","name":"wrxsv","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}